-- Chapter 9, Section 9.5.7 — SQL placeholder syntax (#309).
-- Features: db_effect, sql_provenance, check_error.
--
-- The SQL is literal (so no E207), but it uses a numbered placeholder (?2).
-- Vera's params argument is a positional Array<Option<String>>, so only
-- anonymous ? placeholders have a well-defined binding; numbered (?NNN) and
-- named (:name) forms are rejected at COMPILE time (E209).
public fn numbered(-> @Result<Array<Array<Option<String>>>, String>)
  requires(true)
  ensures(true)
  effects(<DB>)
{
  DB.query("SELECT ?2", [Some("x")])
}
